1
00:00:05,757 --> 00:00:09,400
Hold a coin in your palm. It
is cool, and it has weight.

2
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:11,931
It seems obvious that it is simply there.

3
00:00:12,745 --> 00:00:16,917
We carry two mistakes about
appearances, and they mirror each other.

4
00:00:16,997 --> 00:00:18,765
The first is the familiar one.

5
00:00:18,845 --> 00:00:22,828
We take what we see and touch to
have a fixed nature of its own,

6
00:00:22,908 --> 00:00:26,659
waiting to be found. This
habit is called reification.

7
00:00:26,739 --> 00:00:28,589
It rarely feels like a view.

8
00:00:28,669 --> 00:00:31,338
It feels like the plain
fact that things are there.

9
00:00:32,154 --> 00:00:34,112
The second mistake is quieter.

10
00:00:34,192 --> 00:00:36,803
Having heard that things
lack a fixed nature,

11
00:00:36,883 --> 00:00:42,101
we picture them as faint and ghostly,
like shadows that could be brushed aside.

12
00:00:42,181 --> 00:00:43,895
But the coin is not faint.

13
00:00:43,975 --> 00:00:46,345
It is vivid and solid in its working.

14
00:00:47,158 --> 00:00:52,119
Both mistakes share one assumption: that
being solid and being empty cannot go

15
00:00:52,199 --> 00:00:54,610
together. Four points loosen it.

16
00:00:55,442 --> 00:00:57,604
The first is mutual dependence.

17
00:00:57,684 --> 00:01:00,226
Nothing is long or short by itself.

18
00:01:00,306 --> 00:01:03,786
A stick is long beside a
pebble and short beside a tree.

19
00:01:03,866 --> 00:01:07,074
A person is a parent only
because there is a child.

20
00:01:07,154 --> 00:01:10,607
Your car is its wheels,
its engine, the road,

21
00:01:10,687 --> 00:01:12,563
its purpose and its name.

22
00:01:12,643 --> 00:01:16,966
Gather those relations, and no car
is found lying underneath them.

23
00:01:17,046 --> 00:01:19,887
And this is not a new
ground made of relations.

24
00:01:19,967 --> 00:01:23,668
The relations are as empty
as the things they relate.

25
00:01:24,486 --> 00:01:29,515
The second point is that empty appearances
are not flimsy. Nor are they harmless.

26
00:01:29,595 --> 00:01:33,088
A car has no essence that makes
it a car from its own side.

27
00:01:33,168 --> 00:01:36,933
Yet when it swerves into a
crowd, the injuries are real.

28
00:01:37,013 --> 00:01:40,208
Its emptiness does not
reduce the consequences.

29
00:01:40,288 --> 00:01:41,988
It is part of why they follow.

30
00:01:42,068 --> 00:01:46,499
In a dream, a falling stone
is as heavy as any stone.

31
00:01:46,579 --> 00:01:49,270
Emptiness is not a dimming of appearance.

32
00:01:49,350 --> 00:01:51,041
It is the way appearance is.

33
00:01:51,874 --> 00:01:55,585
The third point is that things
work without a hidden substance.

34
00:01:55,665 --> 00:01:59,933
A bridge carries traffic, though
no single part of it is the bridge.

35
00:02:00,013 --> 00:02:03,465
Steel, deck, supports
and name work together,

36
00:02:03,545 --> 00:02:05,137
and a truck can cross.

37
00:02:05,217 --> 00:02:09,661
The conditions that hold it up are
patterns too, named in the same way.

38
00:02:09,741 --> 00:02:14,634
Nāgārjuna presses this point in the
first chapter of his Middle Way verses.

39
00:02:14,714 --> 00:02:18,615
Search the conditions for a
fixed ground and none is found,

40
00:02:18,695 --> 00:02:20,793
yet the bridge still holds.

41
00:02:21,614 --> 00:02:24,972
The fourth point is habit,
what the tradition calls karma.

42
00:02:25,052 --> 00:02:29,129
What appears to each mind is shaped
by the tendencies it has gathered.

43
00:02:29,209 --> 00:02:31,647
People see water as something to drink.

44
00:02:31,750 --> 00:02:36,426
Fish see it as home. In dim light,
a coiled rope becomes a snake,

45
00:02:36,506 --> 00:02:41,453
and your heart pounds. Look again,
and the snake leaves nothing behind.

46
00:02:41,533 --> 00:02:45,787
The fear was built from habit,
yet it was real in its effects.

47
00:02:45,867 --> 00:02:49,034
Habit is not a hidden
cause behind appearances.

48
00:02:49,114 --> 00:02:50,995
It belongs to the same web.

49
00:02:51,810 --> 00:02:54,094
So two errors fall away together.

50
00:02:54,174 --> 00:02:58,130
Nothing stands behind appearances,
holding them in place.

51
00:02:58,210 --> 00:03:02,876
And appearances without such a
ground are not unreal or disposable.

52
00:03:03,694 --> 00:03:06,563
The coin is still cool
and heavy in the hand.

53
00:03:06,643 --> 00:03:11,852
It is vivid, workable and empty,
and it can be held without grasping.

